# Expo UI / Material 3

- Prefer `@expo/ui/jetpack-compose` (and `@expo/material-symbols` for icons) over reinventing Material 3 in RN.
- Use existing Expo UI components first. Only build custom Compose-backed UI later when Expo has no equivalent.
- Keep app `Icon` as the single call-site API; do not add thin header/icon wrappers.
- Android Compose icons need a **native rebuild** after adding `@expo/ui`.
- iOS may keep a temporary fallback until universal/`@expo/ui` SwiftUI parity is adopted.
- Do **not** put Compose `Host`-per-icon on hot paths (tab bar, lists). Prefer **one** `Host` wrapping many Compose children (e.g. `HorizontalFloatingToolbar`), or font icons.
